    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Karl Jenkin’s Palladio takes inspiration from the eponymous sixteenth-century architect Andrea Palladio. Jenkins himself notes that “Two of Palladio&#8217;s hallmarks are mathematical harmony and architectural elements borrowed from classical antiquity,” and Jenkins himself structures the music based on similar mathematic proportions. Inspired by the famous Brandenburg Concertos, the Concerto in E-flat (Dumbarton Oaks) was the &hellip;  ARCHITECTURE AND CONVERSATIONS Read More &raquo;"
      }
    ],
